# aurora.local / packages/backup/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/backup/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/backup/pins.env to adopt.
#
# Every pin below is curated and human-reviewed.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# kopia/kopia — actively maintained, contrary to an initial hunch that
# this might be a "ships only latest" case. Latest stable is v0.23.1
# (2026-06-16, a bugfix release for "a rare race condition which might
# lead to data loss" — worth adopting for that reason alone). Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Note: the v0.23.x
# line also restricts the insecure unauthenticated server to loopback
# binds only — if Kopia's server/UI is reached over the LAN rather than
# purely from localhost, read the v0.23.0 release notes before adopting
# this pin, since that is a behaviour change, not just a bugfix. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_KOPIA=kopia/kopia:0.23.1@sha256:89fd95ee2942880ca00eae964266958a394421ddbdf69bca62e38afc55f5900e
